        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "91190d98-a192-5e3c-a761-1a6f46371534",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Wiener Nationals, Holiday Bowl\n- Organizations: Wienerschnitzel, NCAA Division I Football Bowl Subdivision\n- Places: San Diego, California, Texas, Arizona, Nevada, Southwestern United States, Qualcomm Stadium\n- Topics: dachshund racing, college football bowl games\n\nFacts:\n- The Holiday Bowl has been played annually since 1978 as a post-season NCAA Division I Football Bowl Subdivision college football bowl game at Qualcomm Stadium in San Diego, California.\n- The Wiener Nationals are the United States national dachshund racing championships sponsored by Wienerschnitzel.\n- Regional qualifiers for the Wiener Nationals are held in the Southwestern United States, including California, Texas, Arizona, and Nevada.\n- Every December, the final eight Dachshunds race for the Wiener Nationals national title in San Diego as part of the Holiday Bowl.",
